---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — testmira" description="About this blog">
  <article class="about-content">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p><strong>testmira</strong> is a minimal dark blog built with <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Astro</a>.</p>
    <p>It's designed for clarity and focus — no distractions, just words and ideas.</p>
    <h2>Features</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Dark theme with warm accent colors</li>
      <li>Markdown and MDX support</li>
      <li>HTML embedding in posts</li>
      <li>Fast static site generation</li>
      <li>Deployed on Cloudflare Pages</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Write Your First Post</h2>
    <p>Create a new <code>.md</code> file in <code>src/content/blog/</code> and start writing. Check the README for the full guide.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-content { padding: 2rem 0; }
  h1 { font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; margin-top: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  p { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.8; }
  ul { margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem 1.5rem; }
  li { margin: 0.5rem 0; line-height: 1.6; }
</style>
